[h1]R.A.T.S. Sensor Views[/h1]
[i]R.A.T.S. – Reconnaissance, Acoustics, Terrain & Signals[/i]

[b]Sit down, Commander. Your cruiser has a real radar room now.[/b]
See who sees what: a phosphor radar scope, a sonar waterfall, a sensor board and live sensor lines on your map.

[quote]▶ [b]Requires[/b] a mod loader: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3835527459]R.A.T.S. Keel[/url] or Anchor Chain, either one
✉ Bugs, ideas, questions: [url=https://hub.sewerlabs.dev/s/sensorviews]R.A.T.S. feedback board[/url]
⭐ A favourite helps other captains find it[/quote]

[h2]✦ New in 0.4[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Scope and sonar show only[/b] what those sensors detect
[*][b]Your own torpedoes on sonar:[/b] steer a wire-guided torpedo by ear
[*][b]Coverage follows the unit[/b] as it moves
[*][b]Runs on 0.9.1[/b] and the flat map (0.8.7)
[/list]

[h2]✦ Highlights[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]A radar that looks like one.[/b] Green phosphor, a glowing sweep, contacts that light up and fade until the next pass
[*][b]Sonar with depth.[/b] Waterfall with baffles, your own noise, a depth strip with thermal layer and seabed
[*][b]Know where you are blind.[/b] Coverage shows where your radar goes dark behind hills
[*][b]Who holds what.[/b] The sensor board: your units across, contacts down, every sensor in a letter
[*][b]Click and fly.[/b] Click a contact on the scope and the camera flies there
[*][b]Everything on one button[/b] at the bottom right
[/list]

[h2]▶ Quick start[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe, and a mod loader if you have none (Keel above)
[*]Switch R.A.T.S. Sensor Views on in Mods
[*]In a mission: the radar button at the right end of the bottom bar
[/olist]
[list]
[*][b]Keys:[/b] Ctrl+Insert, Ctrl+PageUp, Ctrl+PageDown for the windows; Ctrl+Shift+PageUp/PageDown for the map layers
[*][b]Second monitor:[/b] with R.A.T.S. Pop-Out Windows the windows go there too
[/list]

[h2]⚙ Radar scope[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Only what your radar holds;[/b] nothing while it is off
[*][b]Radar horizon ring[/b] for a target altitude you set
[*][b]Blind arcs,[/b] strobes for radars and jammers on you, a LOCK ring for fire control
[*][b]North-up or heading-up,[/b] a cursor with bearing and range, ranges that glide
[/list]

[h2]⚙ Sonar and sensor board[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Waterfall[/b] for the sonar you pick, or Echoes: bearing and range
[*][b]Depth strip:[/b] layer, your depth, the array, contacts at the game's estimated depth
[*][b]Board letters:[/b] R search, F fire control, E ESM, S passive, A active, V visual, M MAD; a click for bearing, range, age
[*][b]The selected unit's sensors:[/b] on or off, damage, arcs, EMCON
[/list]

[h2]⚙ On the map[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Sensor lines:[/b] amber search radar, thick red lock, blue active sonar, dotted visual, wedges for ESM and passive
[*][b]For the selected unit or all units,[/b] per sensor type
[*][b]Coverage:[/b] radar with terrain shadows, ESM, visual, passive sonar; off by default
[/list]

[h2]⚠ Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Display only.[/b] It shows what your sensors already report; the real position of a contact is never shown, missions don't change
[*][b]Passive sonar depth[/b] is the game's rough estimate and can be off by hundreds of feet
[*][b]Many units:[/b] sensor lines for all units can cost frame rate; use the selected unit's lines (a fix is in the works)
[*][b]No game files are changed.[/b] If an update moves a hook, the log says what turned off
[/list]

[h2]⚙ Install and game versions[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Run in the game on 0.9.1[/b] (build 261112): coverage in Red Sea Breakout, under R.A.T.S. Keel
[*][b]0.8.7 (flat map):[/b] checked offline; the right build switches on by itself
[*][b]Settings:[/b] [i]BepInEx\config\dev.sewerlabs.seapowersensorviews.cfg[/i]
[*][b]More:[/b] [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerSensorViews]README on GitHub[/url]
[/list]

